on":"Draws clear, practical route maps under pressure, adapting them as conditions change.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_tovan_reed","name":"Tovan Reed","role":"supporting","description":"A senior Bridge Warden raised among the forge-pits of Emberroost, Tovan learned to braid cloudstone cables by watching generations of engineers work. Broad-shouldered and soft-spoken, he wears a heat-shielded apron and keeps small lengths of test braid tucked in his belt. He has maintained bridges through lean seasons, but his habit of carrying every burden himself has made him slow to accept help from the young cartographer assigned to the repair.","motivation":"Protect the people who depend on the bridges and honor the Wardens' oath to maintain them.","goal":"Complete the repair with the cloudstone available before the next season makes the crossing more dangerous.","flaw":"He is overprotective and hides the full risk of a repair rather than letting others share responsibility.","internal_conflict":"Tovan believes that a good Warden must be the one who absorbs every danger, but he knows that working alone can leave the whole network less safe.","external_conflict":"The repair needs cloudstone braid from Emberroost, accurate route information from Silverspine, and a safe crossing despite Cartel tolls and unsettled winds.","arc":"Tovan begins determined to shoulder the repair alone and keep Lyra away from its hazards. When a shifting route leaves his crew unable to reach the work site without her updated chart, he must choose between concealing the danger and trusting her with the decision. He shares the risks and lets Lyra help redirect the repair, ending as a Warden who protects the bridges by building a team rather than acting as its sole shield.","personality_traits":["patient","protective","practical","reserved"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone braiding","description":"Judges and repairs woven cloudstone cables using the tools and shielded forge-pits of Emberroost.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Bridge assessment","description":"Recognizes strain and weaknesses in a skybridge by examining its cables and supports.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_sella_morne","name":"Sella Morne","role":"antagonist","description":"A sharp-minded Drift Cartel route broker based at Mistral Docks, Sella grew up watching merchants bargain over crossings that could vanish with a change of wind. Neatly dressed and rarely without a ledger, she knows the shipping lanes and the cost of every delay. She argues that strict tolls keep trade predictable, but her faith in orderly accounts has made her dismiss how those costs burden the Hollow Circle and obstruct essential bridge repairs.","motivation":"Preserve the Cartel's control of trade lanes and prevent the archipelago from slipping into disorder.","goal":"Collect the Cartel's skybridge tolls and secure its authority over shipping routes, including those needed by the repair crew.","flaw":"She reduces people and their needs to figures in a ledger, assuming that a fair-looking rule has fair results.","internal_conflict":"Sella wants to believe her work protects the realm from another season of isolation, yet she fears that loosening the Cartel's grip will make her influence—and her ability to prevent chaos—irrelevant.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's rising tolls intensify the Toll War with the Bridge Wardens and the Grain Levy dispute with the Hollow Circle, while Lyra's repair mission needs passage through controlled routes.","arc":"Sella begins convinced that enforcing every toll is the only way to keep trade stable. When her restrictions delay the bridge repair and threaten the grain shipments that sustain the isles, she must choose whether to protect the ledger or allow the crew and Hollow Circle a crossing. She grants passage and accepts scrutiny of the 