{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_sera_vane","name":"Sera Vane","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","description":"Sera is a courier raised among the crowded berths and basalt ledges of Mistral Docks, where she learned that a reliable route can matter more than a powerful patron. Lean and quick-moving, she wears a weather-scuffed flight coat patched with old shipping marks and keeps her hair cropped short to stay clear of rigging. While carrying a sealed dispatch across the habitat network, she finds a message embedded in an old bridge component, apparently left by the builders who first joined the drifting islands. Its contents may reveal why the habitats were made and what the dying star means for their future.","motivation":"She wants people who depend on the routes to have access to the truth, rather than letting the Drift Cartel decide what they are allowed to know.","goal":"Deliver the builders' message to Silverspine Academy and help establish whether it contains actionable information before the Cartel can suppress it.","flaw":"Sera treats self-reliance as a virtue even when refusing help puts others at risk.","internal_conflict":"She fears that accepting obligations to others will cost her the freedom that has kept her safe.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel wants the message contained, while the Bridge Wardens distrust interference with old bridge components; pursuing it also risks adding wind-debt she cannot repay within the season.","arc":"Sera begins as a courier who avoids lasting commitments and sees every crossing as a private bargain. When the Cartel demands that she surrender the message at Mistral Docks and a Warden warns that removing its component could endanger a skybridge, she chooses to entrust the evidence to the Warden and help verify it at Silverspine instead of fleeing alone. She ends willing to share both the risk and the wind-debt with people who need the truth.","personality_traits":["observant","self-reliant","wry","restless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Route memory","description":"Remembers shifting travel routes and landmarks well enough to navigate between known isles without relying on a current chart.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Cargo negotiation","description":"Can bargain over delivery terms and read when a merchant is hiding a toll or obligation.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tovan_reed","name":"Tovan Reed","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","description":"Tovan is a Bridge Warden engineer from Emberroost, trained to inspect and maintain the cloudstone cables braided at the forge-island. Broad-shouldered and careful with his hands, he wears a dark, heat-marked work apron over layers suited to the wind, and keeps small tools secured against the danger of losing them aloft. He believes the old bridges are practical works of engineering, not relics to be disturbed for speculation. Sera's discovery forces him to consider that the builders may have left information essential to the habitats' survival.","motivation":"He wants the bridge network to remain safe for the people who depend on it.","goal":"Determine whether the component containing the message can be examined without weakening a skybridge.","flaw":"He mistakes caution for neutrality and is slow to challenge powerful people who claim that secrecy is necessary for safety.","internal_conflict":"He is torn between his duty to protect existing infrastructure and the possibility that preserving the status quo leaves everyone exposed to a greater danger.","external_conflict":"The Cartel pressures the Wardens to surrender the discovery, while Sera's effort to carry it onward could disturb a bridge component before its condition is understood.","arc":"Tovan begins convinced that keeping the message sealed is the safest course. When Cartel pressure makes clear that inaction would hand control of the evidence to merchants without engineering oversight, he chooses to inspect and document the component with Sera rather than surrender it. He ends still cautious about structural risks, but no longer treats deference to powerful factions as a substitute for protecting the bridges.","personality_traits":["methodical","patient","protective","reserved"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable inspection","description":"Recognizes wear and instability in braided cloudstone bridge cables through close visual and tactile examination.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Repair planning","description":"Plans maintenance work around the risks of wind, crossings, and the rule against open flame outside shielded forge-pits.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_elin_marr","name":"Elin Marr","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","description":"Elin is a cartographer at Silverspine Academy who studies how the skybridge network shifts as the isles drift. She is small and sharp-eyed, with ink-stained cuffs, a wind-worn scarf, and folded route charts tucked into every pocket. Her work depends on comparing old records with present crossings, so she recognizes that Sera's recovered message may be evidence left by the original builders rather than an ordinary dispatch. She wants its claims tested against the Academy's charts before anyone makes promises on its behalf.","motivation":"She wants an accurate account of the network's origins and changes, even when the evidence unsettles established histories.","goal":"Compare the builders' message with the Academy's records and determine what it can reliably tell the habitats about their construction.","flaw":"She can become so focused on verifying evidence that she delays decisions others must make under pressure.","internal_conflict":"She wants knowledge to be shared, but fears that an unverified interpretation could provoke dangerous actions across the network.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's attempt to control the discovery and the Wardens' concern about disturbing old infrastructure limit her access to both the message and the physical evidence.","arc":"Elin begins insisting that no account of the builders be shared until every detail has been checked. When the Cartel moves to seize the message and Sera needs an immediate answer, Elin chooses to disclose the evidence she can substantiate while clearly identifying what remains uncertain. She ends committed to careful scholarship that informs urgent choices instead of postponing them indefinitely.","personality_traits":["curious","precise","cautious","persistent"],"abilities":[{"name":"Drift charting","description":"Compares route records and observations to track changes in the skybridge network.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Evidence assessment","description":"Separates documented facts from plausible but unverified interpretations in historical records.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_sera_tovan","source_character_id":"chr_sera_vane","target_character_id":"chr_tovan_reed","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Sera Vane and Tovan Reed disagree over whether the message should travel immediately or remain with the Bridge Wardens until its component is proven safe to handle; their competing duties can either endanger or protect the evidence."},{"id":"rel_tovan_elin","source_character_id":"chr_tovan_reed","target_character_id":"chr_elin_marr","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tovan Reed relies on Elin Marr's charts to assess the bridge network, while Elin depends on his engineering judgment; his caution can restrict the evidence she needs to verify the builders' message."},{"id":"rel_elin_sera","source_character_id":"chr_elin_marr","target_character_id":"chr_sera_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Elin Marr needs Sera Vane to bring the message to Silverspine, but Sera's urgency conflicts with Elin's insistence on distinguishing verified facts from uncertain claims."}]}
</Output>
