ords threaten the reliability of his maintenance roster, while Mara needs him to confirm a timeline that may draw retaliation.","arc":"Orin begins keeping his records strictly technical and refusing to discuss the Cartel's pressure on repair schedules. When Mara shows him that a disputed crossing falls during a documented bridge closure, he must decide whether to let the roster be quietly revised or attest to the original entry. He signs a copy for the investigation, addressing his habit of retreating into neutrality; by the end he is willing to defend the record publicly while continuing to prioritize bridge safety.","personality_traits":["Practical","Stoic","Protective","Unshowy"],"abilities":[{"name":"Bridge inspection","description":"Recognizes signs of strain, repair, or closure in cloudstone cables and their fittings.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Maintenance records","description":"Keeps detailed rosters that establish when routes were inspected, repaired, or unavailable.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_ilyan","source_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","target_character_id":"chr_ilyan_rusk","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Mara Venn investigates Ilyan Rusk's blackmail scheme, while Ilyan tries to discredit her findings and preserve his false alibi."},{"id":"rel_ilyan_tessa","source_character_id":"chr_ilyan_rusk","target_character_id":"chr_tessa_vale","relationship_type":"blackmailer","description":"Ilyan Rusk uses Tessa Vale's coerced chart alteration and private correspondence to keep her from correcting the route record behind his alibi."},{"id":"rel_tessa_mara","source_character_id":"chr_tessa_vale","target_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","relationship_type":"reluctant_ally","description":"Tessa Vale gives Mara Venn the chart evidence needed to test Ilyan's alibi, but fears Mara will expose her role in the original alteration."},{"id":"rel_orin_mara","