{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_venn","name":"Mara Venn","role":"protagonist","description":"Mara Venn is a private investigator who works the crowded routes and damp basalt ledges of Mistral Docks. Once a meticulous clerk for the Drift Cartel, she left after watching honest records get bent to protect powerful merchants. She keeps her dark hair pinned beneath a weather-stained hood, wears a patched coat with deep pockets for notes, and carries a small ledger of her own. She knows that a crossing leaves both a wind-debt and a trail of witnesses, but her reputation for suspecting everyone makes people wary of helping her.","motivation":"She wants the truth to survive even when powerful people can pay to bury it.","goal":"Identify who is blackmailing Cartel merchants and establish a verifiable account of where each suspect was when the threats were delivered.","flaw":"She treats trust as a weakness and often withholds evidence from the very people who could corroborate it.","internal_conflict":"She wants to believe that careful evidence can protect ordinary people, but her years inside the Cartel taught her that records are often tools of the powerful.","external_conflict":"The blackmailer has manipulated crossing records and recruited frightened witnesses, while the Cartel pressures Mara to stop investigating before its toll dealings are exposed.","arc":"Mara begins convinced that only her private notes are reliable. When Tessa risks her standing at Silverspine Academy to correct a chart that undermines Mara's theory, Mara must choose whether to share her evidence and let others test it. She builds a corroborated alibi from the corrected chart, crossing debts, and Orin's maintenance records; by the end she still questions easy assurances, but no longer mistakes isolation for rigor.","personality_traits":["Observant","Sardonic","Persistent","Guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cross-examination","description":"Finds gaps in a witness's timeline by comparing their account with crossing obligations and other records.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Dockside rapport","description":"Earns candid details from port workers by listening closely and remembering who owes what to whom.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks"},{"id":"chr_ilyan_rusk","name":"Ilyan Rusk","role":"antagonist","description":"Ilyan Rusk is a discreet broker at Mistral Docks who learned to turn shipping schedules and private correspondence into leverage. He presents himself as a careful merchant in an immaculate, dark coat, with polished boots that never seem to touch the mud. A Drift Cartel associate, he knows how to make a threat sound like a reasonable offer and prefers to let other people take the risks his schemes create. He has been blackmailing Cartel traders to redirect toll payments and silence anyone who notices the altered accounts.","motivation":"He wants security and influence in a trade system where the Cartel's fortunes can shift with every change in the wind.","goal":"Keep his blackmail scheme hidden long enough to secure control over a profitable share of the Cartel's toll arrangements.","flaw":"He believes every relationship can be reduced to a debt, a secret, or a price.","internal_conflict":"He wants recognition as a self-made power, yet depends on threats and stolen confidence because he fears that honest work would leave him insignificant.","external_conflict":"Mara is testing his alibi against crossing debts and shipping records, while his leverage over Tessa risks collapsing if she chooses to correct the chart he relies on.","arc":"Ilyan begins confident that fear will keep every witness in line. When Tessa publicly corrects the route chart that supports his claimed alibi, he must choose between exposing her private correspondence to preserve his cover or letting the discrepancy stand. He chooses to threaten her, making his coercion clear to Mara and the Wardens; by the end his network of leverage is exposed, and his effort to command respect has left him without anyone willing to vouch for him.","personality_traits":["Polished","Patient","Controlling","Resentful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Schedule manipulation","description":"Uses his knowledge of shipping routines to make a false timeline seem plausible.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Coercive persuasion","description":"Turns private information into carefully phrased threats that pressure people to cooperate.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel"},{"id":"chr_tessa_vale","name":"Tessa Vale","role":"supporting","description":"Tessa Vale is a cartographer at Silverspine Academy, where she studies how the shifting skybridge network changes with the drift. She is slight, ink-smudged, and usually wrapped in a practical wool shawl with chart tubes strapped across her back. Her work is precise, but she once adjusted a route annotation at Ilyan's request after he threatened to reveal a personal debt. That alteration helped him claim an alibi, and she has spent months fearing that any correction will make her look complicit.","motivation":"She wants to preserve the integrity of her charts and stop her mistake from endangering other people.","goal":"Correct the route record and give Mara enough reliable information to test Ilyan's alibi.","flaw":"She delays difficult disclosures until she can imagine a version that leaves her reputation untouched.","internal_conflict":"She believes accurate maps are a public responsibility, but fears that admitting her own alteration will cost her place at the Academy.","external_conflict":"Ilyan's blackmail keeps her quiet, and the shifting bridge network makes it difficult to prove which chart annotation was accurate at the time of a crossing.","arc":"Tessa begins hiding behind technical uncertainty to avoid admitting she altered a route annotation. When Ilyan threatens to publish her correspondence if she corrects it, she chooses to amend the chart openly and explain the original alteration to Mara. The disclosure gives Mara a sound basis to challenge Ilyan's alibi; by the end Tessa accepts accountability and becomes a more credible keeper of the Academy's records.","personality_traits":["Exacting","Anxious","Conscientious","Reserved"],"abilities":[{"name":"Route reconstruction","description":"Compares successive charts and wind observations to determine which bridges could have been crossed during a given interval.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Cartographic memory","description":"Recalls small differences between route markings and the conditions under which they were recorded.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_orin_pell","name":"Orin Pell","role":"supporting","description":"Orin Pell is a Bridge Warden engineer stationed at Emberroost, where he inspects cloudstone cables and keeps records of repairs. Broad-shouldered and soot-marked from shielded forge-pits, he wears a weatherproof apron over a Warden's work coat and carries a bundle of repair tags instead of a weapon. He is blunt about the danger of careless crossings and skeptical of merchants who treat bridge safety as a line item. His maintenance roster can confirm when a route was closed, but he has kept quiet about suspicious toll pressure to avoid worsening the Toll War.","motivation":"He wants the skybridges kept safe without letting merchants turn their maintenance into another excuse for exploitation.","goal":"Provide an accurate maintenance timeline that helps identify which crossings were physically possible.","flaw":"He mistakes silence for neutrality and avoids taking a public position until damage is already done.","internal_conflict":"He is sworn to maintain the network for everyone, but fears that challenging the Cartel will make the Wardens' work harder and the bridges less safe.","external_conflict":"Cartel toll disputes and pressure on Warden records threaten the reliability of his maintenance roster, while Mara needs him to confirm a timeline that may draw retaliation.","arc":"Orin begins keeping his records strictly technical and refusing to discuss the Cartel's pressure on repair schedules. When Mara shows him that a disputed crossing falls during a documented bridge closure, he must decide whether to let the roster be quietly revised or attest to the original entry. He signs a copy for the investigation, addressing his habit of retreating into neutrality; by the end he is willing to defend the record publicly while continuing to prioritize bridge safety.","personality_traits":["Practical","Stoic","Protective","Unshowy"],"abilities":[{"name":"Bridge inspection","description":"Recognizes signs of strain, repair, or closure in cloudstone cables and their fittings.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Maintenance records","description":"Keeps detailed rosters that establish when routes were inspected, repaired, or unavailable.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_ilyan","source_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","target_character_id":"chr_ilyan_rusk","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Mara Venn investigates Ilyan Rusk's blackmail scheme, while Ilyan tries to discredit her findings and preserve his false alibi."},{"id":"rel_ilyan_tessa","source_character_id":"chr_ilyan_rusk","target_character_id":"chr_tessa_vale","relationship_type":"blackmailer","description":"Ilyan Rusk uses Tessa Vale's coerced chart alteration and private correspondence to keep her from correcting the route record behind his alibi."},{"id":"rel_tessa_mara","source_character_id":"chr_tessa_vale","target_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","relationship_type":"reluctant_ally","description":"Tessa Vale gives Mara Venn the chart evidence needed to test Ilyan's alibi, but fears Mara will expose her role in the original alteration."},{"id":"rel_orin_mara","source_character_id":"chr_orin_pell","target_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","relationship_type":"witness","description":"Orin Pell provides Mara Venn with the maintenance roster that can confirm whether the disputed skybridge was open during Ilyan's claimed crossing."}]}
