{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_ilyra_vane","name":"Ilyra Vane","role":"protagonist","description":"A salvage captain who grew up around the crowded moorings of Mistral Docks, Ilyra learned to judge a vessel by the debts attached to it as much as by its hull. She took the Drift Cartel's contract to board the vanished luxury liner and recover its cargo before another crew could claim it. Her weather-scored coat is carefully mended, and she keeps her hair bound beneath a dark scarf so nothing catches in rigging or passageways.","motivation":"To secure enough salvage to free her crew from the Drift Cartel's leverage.","goal":"Recover the liner's valuable cargo and bring every living crew member back to Mistral Docks.","flaw":"She treats people as liabilities to manage and hides crucial risks until she can control them.","internal_conflict":"She wants to protect her crew but believes that sharing responsibility will cost her command.","external_conflict":"The fog-bound liner is not empty, and the Drift Cartel expects Ilyra to deliver its cargo regardless of what the crew encounters.","arc":"Ilyra begins by withholding the liner's dangers and treating the salvage as a calculation. When the ghostly steward seals the route back and her crew must choose between the cargo and a trapped shipmate, she gives up the most valuable haul to lead a joint escape. She ends willing to share decisions and accept a smaller recovery rather than make her crew pay for her secrecy.","personality_traits":["pragmatic","commanding","guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Salvage judgment","description":"Can quickly assess a vessel's structure, likely hazards, and which valuable-looking objects are unsafe to disturb.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Crew command","description":"Keeps a frightened team coordinated under pressure, though she must learn to make that coordination mutual.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel"},{"id":"chr_tovan_reed","name":"Tovan Reed","role":"supporting","description":"A Bridge Warden cable engineer from Emberroost, Tovan was assigned to Ilyra's salvage crew because he understands the strains that keep a sky-vessel and its rigging intact. His sleeves are burn-scarred from shielded forge-pits, and he wears a small bundle of cloudstone braid at his wrist as a reminder that careless work can endanger more than one person. He is methodical, observant, and uncomfortable when a task has no reliable measurements.","motivation":"To prove that careful engineering can keep people safe even when the rules and materials are unfamiliar.","goal":"Find a way to stabilize the liner's failing rigging long enough for the crew to escape.","flaw":"He clings to procedure when circumstances demand a fast, imperfect choice.","internal_conflict":"He fears that acting without certainty will make him responsible for another avoidable loss.","external_conflict":"The liner's rigging and interior supports are failing in the fog, while the ghostly steward obstructs the crew's attempts to reach safe passage.","arc":"Tovan begins by insisting on inspecting every support before anyone moves, even as the ship shifts around them. When the steward traps Ilyra beyond a buckling passage, Tovan chooses to cut a damaged line before he can fully verify the structure, then directs the crew to share the load. He ends able to act on informed judgment rather than waiting for impossible certainty.","personality_traits":["precise","conscientious","reserved"],"abilities":[{"name":"Rigging assessment","description":"Recognizes strain, weak points, and likely failures in cables and structural supports.","category":"technological"}],"home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_sella_quill","name":"Sella Quill","role":"supporting","description":"A cartographer trained at Silverspine Academy, Sella was hired to interpret the liner's old route records and keep the salvage crew oriented when the fog erased familiar bearings. She carries a case of marked charts and has ink stains along the side of her hand. Her curiosity is genuine, but she has built a reputation on being the person with the answer and dislikes admitting when a map no longer applies.","motivation":"To understand why the liner vanished and what its route can reveal about the shifting network of travel between the isles.","goal":"Compare the liner's records with her charts and identify a safe way back to Mistral Docks.","flaw":"She trusts recorded knowledge more than the people experiencing danger in front of her.","internal_conflict":"She wants to make a meaningful discovery but fears that uncertainty will expose the limits of her expertise.","external_conflict":"The liner's records point the crew deeper into the fog, and the ghostly steward uses familiar routes to mislead them.","arc":"Sella begins by treating the liner's records as an authoritative map. When she realizes the steward is exploiting those records to send the crew in circles, she discards her planned route and follows Tovan's observations and Ilyra's judgment instead. She ends with a partial, honestly qualified chart and a stronger respect for knowledge gathered together rather than claimed alone.","personality_traits":["curious","analytical","proud"],"abilities":[{"name":"Chart interpretation","description":"Reads route records and recognizes inconsistencies between a chart and observed conditions.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_marlow_vesper","name":"Marlow Vesper","role":"antagonist","description":"Once the chief steward aboard the luxury liner, Marlow vanished with the ship decades ago and now appears as a pale, formal presence in its fog-dimmed corridors. His immaculate uniform is unchanged, though its edges blur into the haze, and his rehearsed courtesy never reaches his hollow eyes. He clings to the duties of his old position as if the ship were still carrying guests who must be kept comfortable and aboard.","motivation":"To preserve the liner's ordered world and avoid facing what happened to the people in his care.","goal":"Keep the salvage crew aboard and restore the ship's routines by making them take the places of its missing passengers and staff.","flaw":"He mistakes control and ritual for care.","internal_conflict":"He cannot admit that his devotion to keeping order helped prevent anyone from confronting the liner's danger.","external_conflict":"The crew's attempts to leave threaten the only routine he has maintained for decades, so he misdirects them and seals off their routes through the ship.","arc":"Marlow begins by presenting himself as a courteous guide and enforcing the liner's routines. When Ilyra abandons the cargo to free a trapped crewmate and refuses to let his threats divide them, Marlow must choose whether to keep the crew imprisoned or relinquish the role that has defined him. He finally stops blocking their escape, confronting the possibility that care requires letting people go.","personality_traits":["formal","possessive","evasive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Fogbound presence","description":"Can appear and vanish within the liner's fog and make familiar passages seem to lead elsewhere.","category":"supernatural"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_ilyra_tovan","source_character_id":"chr_ilyra_vane","target_character_id":"chr_tovan_reed","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ilyra Vane relies on Tovan Reed to judge the liner's failing supports, but her habit of withholding risks clashes with his insistence on understanding them before acting."},{"id":"rel_sella_ilyra","source_character_id":"chr_sella_quill","target_character_id":"chr_ilyra_vane","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Sella Quill challenges Ilyra Vane's decisions when they contradict the route records, forcing Sella to choose between her charts and the crew's immediate experience."},{"id":"rel_marlow_ilyra","source_character_id":"chr_marlow_vesper","target_character_id":"chr_ilyra_vane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Marlow Vesper sees Ilyra Vane's plan to leave as a threat to his control of the liner, while Ilyra recognizes his courteous guidance as a trap."},{"id":"rel_tovan_sella","source_character_id":"chr_tovan_reed","target_character_id":"chr_sella_quill","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tovan Reed's observations help Sella Quill test the liner's misleading records, though he distrusts her tendency to defer to the charts."}]}
