{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_tamsin_reed","name":"Tamsin Reed","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","description":"Tamsin Reed grew up among the Hollow Circle's windmills, learning to read shifting currents and the signs of plants that thrive where old stone meets soil. Years ago, she guided a salvage crew across a neglected skybridge; when a sudden gust snapped its weakened span, she escaped while two companions were stranded on the far side. She has since kept to the familiar paths around The Hollow, wearing a patched green coat, a weather-stained map case, and a braid threaded with small seed pods.","motivation":"Make amends for abandoning her stranded companions without pretending the past can be undone.","goal":"Lead the expedition through the jungle growth at The Hollow to reach the buried ruins and bring back proof of what lies there.","flaw":"She treats every risk as hers alone to judge and withholds information when she fears others will make a dangerous choice.","internal_conflict":"She wants to believe she can guide people again, but fears that accepting their trust will make her responsible for another loss.","external_conflict":"The jungle's fast-growing vines and unstable old stone obscure the route, while the Drift Cartel's agent presses the expedition to hurry before their passage and supplies run out.","arc":"Tamsin begins guarded and convinced that keeping decisions to herself protects the crew. When a vine-choked crossing gives way and the party must choose between a risky shortcut and repaying their wind-debt with labor to secure a safer bridge, she reveals her full route notes and lets the others decide together. She ends willing to guide as a partner rather than as the sole authority, confronting her habit of hiding risks instead of sharing them.","personality_traits":["observant","wary","resourceful","dry-humored"],"abilities":[{"name":"Current reading","description":"Recognizes changes in wind and can judge when a skybridge crossing is becoming unsafe.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Jungle navigation","description":"Finds passable routes through dense growth by tracking light, water, and plant patterns.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_vargo_senn","name":"Vargo Senn","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","description":"Vargo Senn is a Drift Cartel factor who built his standing by turning uncertain journeys into predictable ledgers of tolls, cargo, and deadlines. He joined the expedition to secure whatever evidence or valuables the ruins might yield, and to ensure the Cartel controls the story before its rivals do. Neatly dressed even on muddy trails, he carries a brass tally case and keeps his dark hair trimmed close against the wind.","motivation":"Preserve his influence within the Cartel by proving he can turn a dangerous venture into a profitable one.","goal":"Claim the expedition's discoveries for the Cartel and return before the cost of transport and supplies exceeds his authority to spend.","flaw":"He mistakes control and leverage for security, and discounts people whose contributions cannot be easily measured.","internal_conflict":"He wants recognition as a capable leader, yet fears that acting without a contract or guarantee will expose how little power he has on his own.","external_conflict":"Tamsin's cautious pace and the overgrown, crumbling route threaten his timetable, while wind-debt obligations make every delay more costly.","arc":"Vargo begins by treating the expedition as a transaction and Tamsin as hired equipment. When a collapsing trail forces him to surrender his carefully guarded supplies so the crew can shore up a crossing and meet its wind-debt, he must choose between protecting his ledger and keeping the expedition alive. He ends more willing to share authority and accept obligations that cannot be repaid as simple cargo or coin.","personality_traits":["calculating","polished","impatient","ambitious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Trade negotiation","description":"Reads competing interests and bargains for passage, provisions, and repayment terms.","category":"social"},{"name":"Route accounting","description":"Tracks supplies, costs, and wind-debt obligations across a journey.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_elin_marr","name":"Elin Marr","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","description":"Elin Marr is a Bridge Warden engineer from Emberroost, trained to inspect cloudstone cables and repair spans before their failures become disasters. She signed on after hearing that the expedition's route passes old, neglected structures, hoping to keep the group from treating every bridge as disposable. Her sleeves are always rolled up, her copper hair is cropped short, and a coil of measuring cord hangs at her hip.","motivation":"Keep people alive by treating maintenance as a shared duty rather than an afterthought.","goal":"Assess the expedition's bridges and leave each crossing safer than the crew found it.","flaw":"She clings to procedure even when the conditions have changed faster than the rules can account for.","internal_conflict":"She trusts engineering knowledge but doubts her judgment when the world presents a problem no training prepared her to solve.","external_conflict":"Cartel pressure to move quickly conflicts with the time needed to inspect and secure cloudstone spans, while jungle growth conceals damage beneath the trail.","arc":"Elin begins by insisting that every crossing follow standard Warden procedure. When a vine-covered span starts to fail before a full inspection is possible, she chooses to combine her measurements with Tamsin's current reading and the crew's labor instead of waiting for ideal conditions. She ends able to adapt her expertise to the people and terrain at hand without abandoning her responsibility for safety.","personality_traits":["methodical","steadfast","practical","earnest"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone inspection","description":"Detects strain and weak points in skybridge cables and fittings.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Emergency rigging","description":"Uses available materials to brace or stabilize a damaged crossing.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_osa_bell","name":"Osa Bell","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","description":"Osa Bell is a Hollow Circle miller and seed keeper whose family preserved hardy crops through the Great Calm. She joins the expedition because the jungle growth is spreading near familiar windmill paths, and she suspects the ruins' stones and water channels are changing how the plants take root. Osa is broad-shouldered, sun-browned, and carries a cloth satchel of seeds and small tools rather than weapons.","motivation":"Protect The Hollow's food supply and keep the Circle from being treated as a mere source of provisions.","goal":"Determine what is driving the jungle's advance and bring back practical knowledge that can help the Hollow Circle respond.","flaw":"She assumes that outsiders will exploit local knowledge unless she first limits what she shares.","internal_conflict":"She wants the expedition to succeed for her community, but fears that helping strangers will give the Drift Cartel another way to control the Hollow.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's grain levy makes supplies a point of contention, and the crew's urgency risks trampling the ground and water sources Osa is trying to understand.","arc":"Osa begins by guarding her knowledge and treating every request for supplies as a possible Cartel maneuver. When the crew must choose between taking the Hollow Circle's remaining provisions and spending time harvesting safely along the overgrown route, she shares her seed-keeping methods and negotiates a fair contribution. She ends prepared to cooperate openly while insisting that the Circle's labor and resources be respected.","personality_traits":["patient","protective","inventive","plainspoken"],"abilities":[{"name":"Seed keeping","description":"Identifies hardy plants and preserves seeds for cultivation under difficult conditions.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Foraging","description":"Finds useful edible plants while avoiding those likely to harm the crew.","category":"other"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_tamsin_vargo","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reed","target_character_id":"chr_vargo_senn","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tamsin Reed and Vargo Senn clash over pace and authority: she prioritizes a safe route and informed choices, while he pushes for a fast, profitable return."},{"id":"rel_elin_tamsin","source_character_id":"chr_elin_marr","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reed","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Elin Marr relies on Tamsin Reed's knowledge of the jungle route, but challenges Tamsin when she withholds risks from the crew."},{"id":"rel_osa_vargo","source_character_id":"chr_osa_bell","target_character_id":"chr_vargo_senn","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Osa Bell distrusts Vargo Senn because his Cartel interests threaten the Hollow Circle's grain and labor; Vargo sees her insistence on fair terms as an obstacle to his schedule."},{"id":"rel_osa_tamsin","source_character_id":"chr_osa_bell","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reed","relationship_type":"friend","description":"Osa Bell and Tamsin Reed share a commitment to protecting The Hollow, though Osa urges Tamsin to include the community in decisions that affect it."}]}
