dical","steadfast","practical","earnest"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone inspection","description":"Detects strain and weak points in skybridge cables and fittings.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Emergency rigging","description":"Uses available materials to brace or stabilize a damaged crossing.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_osa_bell","name":"Osa Bell","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","description":"Osa Bell is a Hollow Circle miller and seed keeper whose family preserved hardy crops through the Great Calm. She joins the expedition because the jungle growth is spreading near familiar windmill paths, and she suspects the ruins' stones and water channels are changing how the plants take root. Osa is broad-shouldered, sun-browned, and carries a cloth satchel of seeds and small tools rather than weapons.","motivation":"Protect The Hollow's food supply and keep the Circle from being treated as a mere source of provisions.","goal":"Determine what is driving the jungle's advance and bring back practical knowledge that can help the Hollow Circle respond.","flaw":"She assumes that outsiders will exploit local knowledge unless she first limits what she shares.","internal_conflict":"She wants the expedition to succeed for her community, but fears that helping strangers will give the Drift Cartel another way to control the Hollow.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's grain levy makes supplies a point of contention, and the crew's urgency risks trampling the ground and water sources Osa is trying to understand.","arc":"Osa begins by guarding her knowledge and treating every request for supplies as a possible Cartel maneuver. When the crew must choose between taking the Hollow Circle's remaining provisions and spending time harvesting safely along the overgrown route, she shares her seed-keeping methods and negotiates a fair contribution. She ends prepared to cooperate openly while insisting that the Circle's labor and resources be respected.","personality_traits":["patient","protective","inventive","plainspoken"],"abilities":[{"name":"Seed keeping","description":"Identifies hardy plants and preserves seeds for cultivation under difficult conditions.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Foraging","description":"Finds useful edible plants while avoiding those likely to harm the crew.","category":"other"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_tamsin_vargo","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reed","target_character_id":"chr_vargo_senn","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tamsin Reed and Vargo Senn clash over pace and authority: she prioritizes a safe route and informed choices, while he pushes for a fast, profitable return."},{"id":"rel_elin_tamsin","source_character_id":"chr_elin_marr","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reed","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Elin Marr relies on Tamsin Reed's knowledge of the jungle route, but challenges Tamsin when she withholds risks from the crew."},{"id":"rel_osa_vargo","source_character_id":"chr_osa_bell","target_character_id":"chr_vargo_senn","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Osa Bell distrusts Vargo Senn because his Cartel interests threaten the Hollow Circle's grain and labor; Vargo sees her insistence on fair terms as an obstacle to his schedule."},{"id":"rel_osa_tamsin","source_character_id":"chr_osa_bell","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reed","relationship_type":"friend","description":"Osa Bell and Tamsin Reed share a commitment to protecting The Hollow, though Osa urges Tamsin to include the community in decisions that affect it."}]}
