oned at Emberroost, Tovan was raised around the forge-pits where cloudstone cables are braided. Years of watching crossings strain the skybridges have made him meticulous about wind-debt and maintenance. Broad-shouldered and soot-marked, he wears a Warden's work harness with carefully coiled tools and keeps his sleeves fastened against stray sparks.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"Keep the skybridges sound before a preventable failure strands another settlement.","goal":"Secure repayment of Nera's crossing debt in time to complete a needed cable repair.","flaw":"He relies on rules as a substitute for listening to the people bound by them.","internal_conflict":"He believes the debt system protects everyone, yet sees that its burdens fall hardest on communities already squeezed by Cartel tolls.","external_conflict":"Nera's overdue wind-debt and the Wardens' limited repair hands compete with the Cartel's rising tolls and the Hollow's need to move grain.","arc":"Tovan begins by treating Nera's debt as a ledger entry and demands repayment without hearing why she crossed. When a cable repair cannot wait and Nera offers her labor instead of abandoning the route chart, he chooses to organize the work with her rather than send her away. He ends still committed to bridge safety, but more willing to interpret repayment in ways that serve the people the bridges connect.","personality_traits":["Exacting","Practical","Duty-bound","Reserved"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable assessment","description":"Recognizes fraying, tension changes, and weak braids in cloudstone skybridge cables.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Forge discipline","description":"Works safely and efficiently around shielded forge-pits, where open flame is permitted.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_nera_tovan","source_character_id":"chr_nera_venn","target_character_id":"chr_tovan_rell","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Nera Venn sees Tovan Rell as the Warden standing between her and the return route; Tovan sees Nera as a traveler who risks treating shared bridges as if their costs belong to someone else. Their dispute over her wind-debt forces each to confront what responsibility to the archipelago requires."}]}
