ermitted by local custom.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_ren_calder","name":"Ren Calder","role":"protagonist","description":"A sharp-tongued shipping broker of Mistral Docks, Ren inherited a modest route ledger rather than the power of the Drift Cartel's merchant princes. He wears a weathered blue coat with hidden pockets full of manifests and keeps his close-cropped hair neatly combed even when the port is in chaos. He knows the shipping lanes intimately, but years of bargaining have taught him to mistake every concession for a future loss.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"Preserve the livelihoods of dock crews and independent traders who cannot survive a prolonged disruption.","goal":"Persuade the Cartel to suspend toll collection on routes needed for emergency bridge repairs.","flaw":"He uses selective truths and private deals to keep control, even when openness would earn allies.","internal_conflict":"Ren wants to be seen as more than a Cartel operator, but fears that acting against the institution will leave him powerless to help anyone.","external_conflict":"Cartel leaders expect him to enforce rising tolls, while the other city delegates see his affiliation as proof that he cannot be trusted.","arc":"Ren begins by trying to trade small, private concessions for influence inside the Cartel. When a blocked repair convoy forces him to choose between protecting his standing and letting essential supplies cross, he releases the relevant shipping records to all three delegations. He ends the story with less control over negotiations but a place at the alliance table earned through candor.","personality_traits":["persuasive","wary","observant","pragmatic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Route accounting","description":"Tracks cargo, tolls, and shipping schedules well enough to expose bottlenecks and costly discrepancies.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Port negotiation","description":"Finds workable terms among crews, 