":"Spots inconsistencies between recorded routes, current conditions, and travelers' reports.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_maelin_ro","name":"Maelin Ro","role":"supporting","description":"A millwright and grain delegate of the Hollow Circle, Maelin keeps the windmills of The Hollow working and knows how much food can be spared without endangering the next harvest. She is broad-shouldered, silver-haired, and usually carries a small ledger bound in worn cloth. Years of quietly feeding the archipelago have made her patient with practical work and impatient with officials who discuss shipments as if they were numbers alone.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"Protect the Hollow's ability to feed its own people and sustain the wider archipelago.","goal":"Win an alliance agreement that exempts emergency grain shipments from the Cartel levy and honors the labour owed for bridge crossings.","flaw":"She delays difficult conversations until she has exhausted every private remedy.","internal_conflict":"Maelin wants to preserve her community's independence, yet recognizes that refusing all outside obligations could leave other isles hungry.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's grain levy strains the Hollow's stores, while wind-debt obligations make it costly to move supplies along the bridges.","arc":"Maelin begins by quietly rationing shipments and hoping the levy dispute will pass without exposing the Hollow's vulnerability. When a damaged route makes it impossible to deliver grain on schedule, she must tell the other delegates exactly what the Circle can and cannot provide. She ends the story as a forthright negotiator who protects the Hollow by making its needs part of the alliance's shared plan.","personality_traits":["patient","practical","protective","plainspoken"],"abilities":[{"name":"Millwrighting","description":"Maintains windmills and diagnoses mechanical faults that threaten grain production.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Storekeeping","description":"Calculates how grain reserves and shipment schedules can support people through disruption.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_tamsin_ren","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_vell","target_character_id":"chr_ren_calder","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tamsin Vell distrusts Ren Calder's Cartel ties and blames toll decisions for delaying bridge inspections; Ren resents her assumption that Wardens should control access without accounting for shipping costs."},{"id":"rel_ren_tamsin","source_character_id":"chr_ren_calder","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_vell","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ren Calder and Tamsin Vell reluctantly work together when the shared safety of the routes becomes more urgent than their dispute over tolls and authority."},{"id":"rel_ilyra_tamsin","source_character_id":"chr_ilyra_senn","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_vell","relationship_type":"colleague","description":"Ilyra Senn and Tamsin Vell share Bridge Warden responsibilities, but Ilyra's maps sometimes contradict Tamsin's inspection records, forcing both to question their assumptions."},{"id":"rel_maelin_ren","source_character_id":"chr_maelin_ro","target_character_id":"chr_ren_calder","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Maelin Ro opposes Ren Calder's Cartel levy on grain, while Ren must negotiate with her to keep food moving through Mistral Docks."},{"id":"rel_maelin_ilyra","source_character_id":"chr_maelin_ro","target_character_id":"chr_ilyra_senn","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Maelin Ro relies on Ilyra Senn's changing-route charts to plan grain shipments, and Ilyra depends on Maelin's practical reports to correct her maps."}]}
