on","description":"Recognizes stress and wear in braided bridge cables from close study.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_dain_merrow","name":"Dain Merrow","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","description":"A veteran cable-braider from Emberroost, Dain has spent decades repairing cloudstone spans and teaching apprentices to respect the wind-debt owed for every crossing. Broad-shouldered and graying, he wears a scarred leather apron over layered work clothes and keeps his tools carefully shielded from open flame. He survived the network attack but lost apprentices in the ensuing failures, leaving him unwilling to trust a repair plan he cannot control.","motivation":"Prevent another generation of bridge workers from being lost to rushed repairs.","goal":"Stabilize the damaged crossings and ensure repair crews receive the labor and goods owed to them.","flaw":"His caution hardens into obstruction when a plan departs from methods he knows.","internal_conflict":"Dain wants to protect his crew, but fears that stepping aside would make him responsible for preventable deaths.","external_conflict":"He lacks enough workers and supplies to restore the network, while the Cartel demands a rapid reopening and the Wardens disagree over which spans to prioritize.","arc":"Dain begins by rejecting Sera's route because its safety has not been proven by his own inspections. When a damaged span leaves his crew with no safe conventional repair option, he chooses to teach Sera the cable tests that could validate her chart. He ends as a cautious collaborator, sharing authority instead of using caution to halt every unfamiliar plan.","personality_traits":["protective","practical","stubborn","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable braiding","description":"Repairs and reinforces cloudstone cables using established Warden techniques.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Crew leadership","description":"Keeps repair crews coordinated