{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_sera_voss","name":"Sera Voss","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","description":"A skybridge cartographer raised among the shifting charts of Silverspine Academy, Sera can read the drift patterns that make a route safe—or deadly. She is spare and sharp-featured, with wind-chapped skin, ink-stained fingers, and a brass lens always hanging at her throat. After an attack crippled the central skybridge network, she found evidence that an overlooked route could reconnect the isolated isles, but the discovery implicates people she once trusted.","motivation":"Keep the stranded settlements connected without sacrificing the people who maintain the bridges.","goal":"Chart and verify a safe route through the damaged network before the next season makes the isolation permanent.","flaw":"She treats uncertainty as a personal failure and hides incomplete findings until she can prove them.","internal_conflict":"Sera believes responsibility means never asking others to risk what she cannot guarantee, even when delay puts more lives in danger.","external_conflict":"The damaged skybridge network has cut off trade and news, while the Bridge Wardens and Drift Cartel dispute who may authorize repairs and crossings.","arc":"Sera begins withholding her uncertain route calculations to avoid being blamed for another failure. When the Cartel's pressure to reopen a dangerous crossing forces her to choose between acting alone and sharing unfinished work, she presents her charts to the Wardens and Hollow Circle for scrutiny. She ends willing to make a decision collectively, accepting that shared risk is safer than solitary certainty.","personality_traits":["observant","methodical","guarded","resolute"],"abilities":[{"name":"Drift charting","description":"Reads shifting wind patterns and maps viable skybridge routes from changing currents.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Cloudstone inspection","description":"Recognizes stress and wear in braided bridge cables from close study.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_dain_merrow","name":"Dain Merrow","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","description":"A veteran cable-braider from Emberroost, Dain has spent decades repairing cloudstone spans and teaching apprentices to respect the wind-debt owed for every crossing. Broad-shouldered and graying, he wears a scarred leather apron over layered work clothes and keeps his tools carefully shielded from open flame. He survived the network attack but lost apprentices in the ensuing failures, leaving him unwilling to trust a repair plan he cannot control.","motivation":"Prevent another generation of bridge workers from being lost to rushed repairs.","goal":"Stabilize the damaged crossings and ensure repair crews receive the labor and goods owed to them.","flaw":"His caution hardens into obstruction when a plan departs from methods he knows.","internal_conflict":"Dain wants to protect his crew, but fears that stepping aside would make him responsible for preventable deaths.","external_conflict":"He lacks enough workers and supplies to restore the network, while the Cartel demands a rapid reopening and the Wardens disagree over which spans to prioritize.","arc":"Dain begins by rejecting Sera's route because its safety has not been proven by his own inspections. When a damaged span leaves his crew with no safe conventional repair option, he chooses to teach Sera the cable tests that could validate her chart. He ends as a cautious collaborator, sharing authority instead of using caution to halt every unfamiliar plan.","personality_traits":["protective","practical","stubborn","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable braiding","description":"Repairs and reinforces cloudstone cables using established Warden techniques.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Crew leadership","description":"Keeps repair crews coordinated under pressure and attentive to bridge safety.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_lyra_quill","name":"Lyra Quill","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","description":"A shipping clerk at Mistral Docks, Lyra knows how the Cartel's manifests, tolls, and wind-debts shape life across the archipelago. She is small and quick-moving, with a close-cropped haircut, a weatherproof coat, and a ledger tucked inside it. The attack wrecked the routes she was paid to schedule, and she has discovered that the Cartel's records conceal how badly the toll system has burdened the isolated isles.","motivation":"Keep essential trade moving while preventing the Cartel from using the crisis to tighten its hold.","goal":"Expose the hidden toll burden and secure a fair accounting of crossings and wind-debts.","flaw":"She relies on private bargains and selective truths, assuming every open disagreement will cost her leverage.","internal_conflict":"Lyra wants to repair the damage done by the Cartel, but fears that losing her position will leave her unable to help anyone.","external_conflict":"Cartel leaders expect her to protect their accounts, while the Hollow Circle resists grain levies and stranded communities need supplies moved across the damaged network.","arc":"Lyra starts by quietly altering individual manifests to ease the burden on a few traders while keeping the Cartel's larger accounts intact. When a blocked grain shipment forces her to choose between another hidden exception and revealing the pattern behind the levies, she shares the records with the Hollow Circle and Wardens. She ends with less private influence but a public role in demanding accountable tolls.","personality_traits":["resourceful","diplomatic","wary","ambitious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Trade accounting","description":"Tracks manifests, tolls, and wind-debts across the shipping records.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Negotiation","description":"Finds workable terms between traders and officials with competing interests.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tomas_reed","name":"Tomas Reed","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","description":"A miller and windmill keeper from the Hollow, Tomas has spent his life turning the isle's harvest into flour for settlements across the archipelago. He is lean, sun-browned, and usually dusted with grain, with a patched coat and a calm voice that carries over the millstones. Since the attack severed reliable routes, he has watched stores dwindle and neighbors argue over whether to share what remains or keep it for their own isle.","motivation":"Make sure hunger does not turn the isolated isles against one another.","goal":"Organize a fair distribution of grain and get supplies moving again without accepting the Cartel's levy.","flaw":"He avoids confrontation so long that resentment grows in the silence.","internal_conflict":"Tomas values the Hollow Circle's mutual aid, but worries that asking others to sacrifice will expose how little he can promise in return.","external_conflict":"The damaged routes block grain shipments, and the Cartel's levy threatens to take food from the very communities that produce it.","arc":"Tomas begins by quietly rationing the Hollow's grain and hoping the dispute will settle before anyone must be refused. When Lyra reveals the levy records and the Circle demands a decision, he publicly argues for a shared distribution plan and rejects the levy despite the risk of retaliation. He ends more willing to confront powerful interests directly while keeping aid rooted in collective consent.","personality_traits":["steady","compassionate","conflict-averse","steadfast"],"abilities":[{"name":"Millwrighting","description":"Maintains windmills and adapts their operation to changing currents.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Harvest planning","description":"Estimates stores and organizes grain distribution through lean seasons.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_sera_dain","source_character_id":"chr_sera_voss","target_character_id":"chr_dain_merrow","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Dain Merrow trained Sera Voss in bridge inspection, but his refusal to trust her unverified route puts their shared duty to the Wardens at odds."},{"id":"rel_lyra_tomas","source_character_id":"chr_lyra_quill","target_character_id":"chr_tomas_reed","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Lyra Quill and Tomas Reed work together to move Hollow grain through the damaged network, while their opposition to the levy risks a confrontation with the Cartel."},{"id":"rel_dain_lyra","source_character_id":"chr_dain_merrow","target_character_id":"chr_lyra_quill","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Dain Merrow distrusts Lyra Quill's Cartel ties and demands that her shipping records be opened before the Wardens commit crews to a reopening plan."}]}
