rms between traders and officials with competing interests.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tomas_reed","name":"Tomas Reed","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","description":"A miller and windmill keeper from the Hollow, Tomas has spent his life turning the isle's harvest into flour for settlements across the archipelago. He is lean, sun-browned, and usually dusted with grain, with a patched coat and a calm voice that carries over the millstones. Since the attack severed reliable routes, he has watched stores dwindle and neighbors argue over whether to share what remains or keep it for their own isle.","motivation":"Make sure hunger does not turn the isolated isles against one another.","goal":"Organize a fair distribution of grain and get supplies moving again without accepting the Cartel's levy.","flaw":"He avoids confrontation so long that resentment grows in the silence.","internal_conflict":"Tomas values the Hollow Circle's mutual aid, but worries that asking others to sacrifice will expose how little he can promise in return.","external_conflict":"The damaged routes block grain shipments, and the Cartel's levy threatens to take food from the very communities that produce it.","arc":"Tomas begins by quietly rationing the Hollow's grain and hoping the dispute will settle before anyone must be refused. When Lyra reveals the levy records and the Circle demands a decision, he publicly argues for a shared distribution plan and rejects the levy despite the risk of retaliation. He ends more willing to confront powerful interests directly while keeping aid rooted in collective consent.","personality_traits":["steady","compassionate","conflict-averse","steadfast"],"abilities":[{"name":"Millwrighting","description":"Maintains windmills and adapts their operation to changing currents.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Harvest planning","description":"Estimates stores and organizes grain distribution through lean 