{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_vell","name":"Mara Vell","role":"protagonist","description":"A Bridge Warden from Emberroost, Mara grew up measuring cable strain beside the forge-pits and learned that a bridge survives through careful work, not miracles. She is lean and broad-shouldered, with soot-dark hair cropped close and old rope burns across her palms. Now she inspects the oldest skybridges, where the traditional ward braces—mundane cloudstone windbreaks and tension frames—are splitting faster than the Wardens can repair them.","motivation":"Keep the failing bridges from taking lives, even if doing so exposes the Wardens' neglect.","goal":"Find which failing ward braces can be stabilized before the next season of wind-debt comes due.","flaw":"She treats every problem as a test of personal endurance and hides evidence of failure until she has a fix.","internal_conflict":"Mara believes that admitting the Wardens cannot protect everyone will make their work—and her own sacrifices—meaningless.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel demands that bridges remain open for toll traffic while the Bridge Wardens lack enough materials and labour to repair the failing wards.","arc":"Mara begins by concealing the worst cracks and trying to shore them up alone. When a heavily tolled crossing buckles under a Cartel convoy, she must choose between hiding the damage again or publicly closing it and revealing the Wardens' shortages. She closes the bridge, forcing the factions to confront the danger, and ends willing to share responsibility rather than stake lives on her solitary competence.","personality_traits":["methodical","stubborn","protective","dry-witted"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable inspection","description":"Can identify stress, fraying, and unsafe load patterns in cloudstone bridge cables by sight and touch.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Emergency rigging","description":"Can improvise temporary supports and harnesses from ordinary bridge-maintenance materials.","category":"physical"}],"home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_tovan_rell","name":"Tovan Rell","role":"antagonist","description":"A senior Drift Cartel factor based at Mistral Docks, Tovan rose from a family of small-time carriers by turning every crossing, delay, and cargo manifest into leverage. He dresses in immaculate weatherproof coats and keeps his silvering hair tied back with a dock ledger ribbon. He has no arcane power or patience for superstition; to him, the old wards are costly infrastructure whose failures can be managed through tariffs and selective closures.","motivation":"Preserve the Cartel's control of shipping lanes and prove that its charter keeps the archipelago orderly.","goal":"Keep the busiest crossings open and force the Wardens to accept Cartel oversight of repair schedules.","flaw":"He mistakes control of records and prices for control of the physical world.","internal_conflict":"Tovan fears that without the Cartel's authority he will become the powerless carrier he once was, so he cannot admit that his policies are worsening the danger.","external_conflict":"Mara's inspections threaten to close toll routes, while the Cartel's rising tolls and grain levy deepen resistance from the Wardens and Hollow Circle.","arc":"Tovan begins convinced that every crisis can be contained by adjusting tolls and controlling information. When a ward failure strands a Cartel shipment near Mistral Docks and his ledgers show that deferred bridge labour helped cause it, he must choose between suppressing the records or releasing them to coordinate repairs. He releases them to avert wider losses, ending with less control but a more honest role in keeping trade moving.","personality_traits":["calculating","polished","patient","defensive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Trade negotiation","description":"Can bargain over cargo schedules, tolls, and repayment terms while keeping several parties in play.","category":"social"},{"name":"Route accounting","description":"Can trace shipping delays and debts across manifests and identify where a supply chain is likely to fail.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel"},{"id":"chr_elin_sorn","name":"Elin Sorn","role":"supporting","description":"A millwright and grain organizer from The Hollow, Elin belongs to the Hollow Circle and knows how a missed shipment turns quickly into empty bins. She is compact and strong from hauling mill parts, with wind-chapped cheeks and a braid threaded with plain bits of twine. She has spent years adapting windmills to the Great Calm's lessons of self-reliance and now sees the failing wards as another reason not to let distant merchants dictate the isles' survival.","motivation":"Protect her community from hunger and from being made dependent on the Cartel.","goal":"Secure a fair grain shipment schedule that includes labour and materials for repairing the threatened crossings.","flaw":"She assumes compromise is simply another name for surrender and can turn allies away with her suspicion.","internal_conflict":"Elin wants the isles to stand on their own, yet she knows The Hollow cannot feed everyone if the bridges fail.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's grain levy and tolls drain the Circle's stores, while unsafe bridges make independent shipments perilous.","arc":"Elin starts by refusing to share the Circle's grain beyond The Hollow, convinced that every concession will be exploited. When the failing wards threaten the route that carries both food and repair supplies, she chooses to provide grain in exchange for a publicly agreed labour schedule rather than wait for the Cartel to dictate terms. She ends still wary of dependence but able to make a practical alliance without giving up her community's voice.","personality_traits":["resourceful","blunt","loyal","wary"],"abilities":[{"name":"Mill repair","description":"Can diagnose and repair windmill gears and other ordinary mechanical equipment.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Supply planning","description":"Can ration grain and organize shipments around changing wind and route conditions.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_tovan","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_tovan_rell","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara Vell sees Tovan Rell's demand to keep toll routes open as a direct threat to bridge safety; Tovan regards her inspections and closures as a challenge to Cartel authority."},{"id":"rel_elin_mara","source_character_id":"chr_elin_sorn","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Elin Sorn can supply grain and practical support for Mara Vell's repairs, but she expects Mara to make the Wardens answerable to the communities that rely on the bridges."},{"id":"rel_tovan_elin","source_character_id":"chr_tovan_rell","target_character_id":"chr_elin_sorn","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Tovan Rell presses the Cartel grain levy on Elin Sorn's community, while Elin organizes resistance and challenges his control of shipping."}]}
</Output>
