{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_lyra_venn","name":"Lyra Venn","role":"protagonist","description":"A cloudstone miner from Emberroost, Lyra has spent years listening for structural weaknesses in the cables she helps extract and shape. She is spare-built, with soot-dark hair usually bound beneath a miner's scarf and pale glints of crystal dust caught in the creases of her hands. When a seam yields a strange, translucent stone she names dreamstone, Lyra is the first to sleep near it—and the first to recognize that the dreams spreading across the isles contain details no single dreamer could know.","motivation":"Keep the dreamstone from being turned into a tool of control, while finding out why its shared dreams seem to remember events no living person witnessed.","goal":"Bring the dreamstone's effects before the Bridge Wardens and secure a careful investigation before the Drift Cartel can claim it.","flaw":"She treats secrecy as protection and withholds crucial information even from people trying to help.","internal_conflict":"The shared dreams offer her a sense of belonging she has never found among the solitary miners, but accepting that comfort means risking her own judgment and memories.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel wants to control the dreamstone and its shipping, while the Wardens fear its presence near the skybridge cables could endanger the network.","arc":"Lyra begins convinced that keeping the discovery secret is the only way to protect it. When a shared dream reveals a threat to a skybridge cable and her silence delays the Wardens' response, she must choose between hiding the stone and exposing what it can do. She shares her evidence with both the Wardens and the affected dreamers, ending as a cautious advocate for collective decisions rather than a solitary keeper.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","personality_traits":["observant","guarded","patient","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable listening","description":"Can detect strain and hidden fractures in cloudstone cables by listening to their vibration.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Dream recall","description":"Remembers shared dreams in unusually precise detail, including images and voices from other dreamers.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_oren_saye","name":"Oren Saye","role":"antagonist","description":"A Drift Cartel factor based at Mistral Docks, Oren rose from a family that paid wind-debts in labor and learned to regard every crossing as a ledger entry waiting to be owned. He dresses in immaculate trade coats with a narrow brass tally-chain at his waist, and keeps his silvering hair trimmed close against the dock winds. Oren sees the dreamstone's colony-wide visions as a way to anticipate dissent, protect cargo, and make the Cartel's tolls seem inevitable.","motivation":"Replace the uncertainty of trade and political resistance with a system he can predict and control.","goal":"Obtain the dreamstone and make its shared dreams a Cartel-controlled source of information.","flaw":"He mistakes information and leverage for genuine understanding of other people.","internal_conflict":"He wants to believe that imposing order will spare the isles from another Great Calm, yet the dreamstone's visions unsettle him with memories and fears that cannot be entered in a ledger.","external_conflict":"The Bridge Wardens oppose Cartel control near the skybridges, and Lyra's knowledge makes it harder for Oren to quietly secure the crystal.","arc":"Oren begins certain that the dreamstone can make every risk legible and manageable. When a shared dream exposes the fear his own toll policies have caused among the islanders, he must decide whether to use that knowledge to tighten his grip or reveal the Cartel's plan. He chooses to disclose the attempt to seize the stone, ending with less control over trade but a first, uncomfortable willingness to hear people without pricing their answers.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","personality_traits":["calculating","polished","ambitious","uneasy"],"abilities":[{"name":"Trade negotiation","description":"Can read competing interests and shape agreements around tolls, cargo, and wind-debts.","category":"social"},{"name":"Pattern forecasting","description":"Uses shipping records and shifting trade patterns to anticipate shortages and political pressure.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_maelin_ro","name":"Maelin Ro","role":"supporting","description":"A Bridge Warden engineer stationed between Emberroost and Silverspine Academy, Maelin is a methodical inspector who has devoted her life to keeping the skybridge network intact. She is broad-shouldered, wears a patched Warden's harness, and marks each cable inspection on a slate with tiny, exact symbols. Maelin once dismissed a miner's warning as rumor; since then she has trusted measurements over testimony, even when the two seem to point in different directions. The dreamstone challenges that habit by giving unrelated people the same impossible image.","motivation":"Keep the skybridges safe without letting fear or speculation dictate engineering decisions.","goal":"Determine whether the dreamstone threatens the cloudstone cables and prevent either the Cartel or the Wardens from using it recklessly.","flaw":"She relies so heavily on verifiable measurements that she discounts testimony until damage is already visible.","internal_conflict":"She fears that trusting uncanny evidence will make her a danger to the very network she has sworn to protect, but dismissing it could repeat the mistake that still haunts her.","external_conflict":"The Wardens need a reliable assessment before the Cartel moves the dreamstone, but the shared dreams resist ordinary testing and time is short.","arc":"Maelin begins insisting that only physical measurements count as evidence. When a shared dream gives Lyra and Maelin the same warning about a cable defect that her instruments have not yet detected, Maelin chooses to halt a crossing and inspect it rather than wait for proof of failure. The inspection confirms the danger, and she ends willing to weigh collective testimony alongside her instruments without abandoning engineering rigor.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","personality_traits":["precise","steadfast","skeptical","conscientious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Bridge assessment","description":"Evaluates cloudstone cable wear and determines which crossings need inspection or repair.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Cartographic memory","description":"Keeps an accurate mental picture of shifting routes and connections across the skybridge network.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_lyra_maelin","source_character_id":"chr_lyra_venn","target_character_id":"chr_maelin_ro","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Lyra trusts Maelin to protect the skybridges but resents her initial skepticism; Maelin needs Lyra's firsthand knowledge even as Lyra's secrecy strains their cooperation."},{"id":"rel_oren_lyra","source_character_id":"chr_oren_saye","target_character_id":"chr_lyra_venn","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Oren seeks to control the dreamstone Lyra discovered, while Lyra sees his plans as a threat to the dreamers and the isles."},{"id":"rel_maelin_oren","source_character_id":"chr_maelin_ro","target_character_id":"chr_oren_saye","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Maelin opposes Oren's effort to take the dreamstone near the skybridge network, deepening the existing struggle between the Bridge Wardens and the Drift Cartel."}]}
