[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_tamsin_reeve","name":"Tamsin Reeve","description":"A precise, restless cartographer at Silverspine Academy, Tamsin grew up watching the skybridges shift with the drift and learned to trust charts more than promises. She keeps her dark hair pinned beneath a weather-stained hood and carries ink-stained route books filled with alternate crossings. When asked to document eight viable passages despite an official limit of four locations, she sees a chance to expose how incomplete records serve the powerful.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"Make the changing skybridge network legible to the people who depend on it, not just those who profit from it.","goal":"Present an honest account of eight possible crossings while keeping the official record within its four-location limit.","flaw":"She treats precision as a substitute for trust and hides uncertainty until it becomes a crisis.","internal_conflict":"Tamsin wants the truth recorded, but fears that showing incomplete or shifting evidence will discredit her work.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel wants route records that justify its tolls, while the Bridge Wardens need accurate information to keep the crossings safe.","arc":"Tamsin begins convinced that a flawless chart can settle the dispute. When a wind shift invalidates one of her carefully guarded routes during a Warden review, she chooses to publish the uncertainty and the competing crossings together. She ends willing to share authority over the record, addressing her habit of hiding doubt and giving travelers evidence they can judge for themselves.","personality_traits":["observant","methodical","guarded","curious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Drift charting","description":"Can compare wind patterns and shifting bridge alignments to identify plausible routes, while recognizing when a chart has become unreliable.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_bram_vell","name":"Bram Vell","description":"A senior Bridge Warden stationed at Emberroost, Bram has spent years inspecting cloudstone braids and paying down his wind-debt through dangerous repair shifts. Broad-shouldered and soot-marked from shielded forge-pits, he trusts sound cables and tested procedures more than political assurances. He regards the proposed tolls as a threat to maintenance, even as he resents the Cartel's influence over who gets to cross.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"Keep the skybridges sound enough that no traveler is lost to neglected maintenance.","goal":"Secure a fair share of crossing revenue for repairs without making safety dependent on Cartel approval.","flaw":"His rigid sense of duty makes him dismiss people whose work is not technical.","internal_conflict":"Bram believes the Wardens must remain above politics, but knows that refusing to engage leaves decisions to the Cartel.","external_conflict":"The Toll War places Warden maintenance needs against the Drift Cartel's rising tolls, while wind-debt obligations leave workers with little freedom to refuse hazardous assignments.","arc":"Bram begins by insisting that the Wardens should answer the toll dispute only with repair records. When Tamsin's shared chart shows that a proposed route would place an avoidable burden on indebted crossing crews, he agrees to testify with her before the Cartel's representatives. He ends using his technical authority to advocate for the workers affected by his decisions, confronting his tendency to separate duty from people.","personality_traits":["steadfast","plainspoken","cautious","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone inspection","description":"Can identify fraying, stress, and unsafe joins in skybridge braids through close inspection and practical repair experience.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_seren_dask","name":"Seren Dask","description":"A shipping factor for the Drift Cartel at Mistral Docks, Seren rose from a family of small traders by learning which currents brought cargo in safely and which promises were worth nothing. Neatly dressed in layered sailcloth, she speaks softly and keeps meticulous toll ledgers. She supports the Cartel's control of shipping lanes because she believes centralized rules prevent the archipelago from repeating the privations of the Great Calm.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"Preserve reliable trade between the isles and prevent another period of isolation.","goal":"Make the Cartel's toll schedule and route records the accepted basis for inter-isle shipping.","flaw":"She mistakes control for stability and assumes that people who resist the Cartel are willing to endanger everyone.","internal_conflict":"Seren fears that loosening the Cartel's grip will revive the helplessness of the Great Calm, yet knows its tolls are making that fear profitable.","external_conflict":"Her effort to enforce rising bridge tolls intensifies the Toll War with the Wardens and helps provoke the Hollow Circle's resistance to the grain levy.","arc":"Seren begins by treating every disagreement as a threat to order. After Tamsin presents conflicting route evidence and the Hollow Circle refuses to let grain shipments be counted as ordinary cargo, Seren chooses to open the toll ledger to scrutiny rather than conceal the disputed charges. She ends still committed to trade but willing to accept limits on Cartel control, challenging her belief that stability requires domination.","personality_traits":["composed","strategic","persuasive","fearful of scarcity"],"abilities":[{"name":"Trade negotiation","description":"Can read the interests behind a shipping dispute and negotiate terms that keep cargo and crews moving.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ila_marr","name":"Ila Marr","description":"A miller and organizer of the Hollow Circle, Ila keeps the windmills of The Hollow working through uneven currents and remembers how the Great Calm taught the isle to rely on its own stores. She is wiry, sun-browned, and usually carries a tally slate dusted with grain. Her careful records make her a trusted voice among farmers, though her suspicion of outside arrangements can isolate the people she means to protect.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"Protect the food stores and bargaining power that let The Hollow survive disruptions.","goal":"Resist the Cartel grain levy without cutting off the archipelago's legitimate access to food.","flaw":"She equates compromise with surrender and keeps crucial information within the Circle for too long.","internal_conflict":"Ila wants her community to remain self-reliant, but understands that isolation can make other isles vulnerable and leave The Hollow alone against the Cartel.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's levy on grain shipments threatens the Hollow Circle's control of its harvest, while the Toll War makes every crossing more costly.","arc":"Ila begins determined to answer the levy with a blanket refusal to ship grain. When the Cartel's toll dispute threatens to obstruct necessary deliveries, she chooses to share the Circle's harvest tallies with Tamsin and negotiate a limited shipment on transparent terms. She ends better able to distinguish cooperation from capitulation, addressing the secrecy and inflexibility that weakened her position.","personality_traits":["resourceful","steadfast","suspicious","communal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Harvest accounting","description":"Can track stores, mill output, and shipment shares closely enough to expose unfair levies without risking the community's reserves.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_tamsin_seren","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reeve","target_character_id":"chr_seren_dask","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tamsin's route evidence challenges Seren's Cartel-approved records; each sees the other's version of the crossings as a threat to the people who rely on it."},{"id":"rel_bram_seren","source_character_id":"chr_bram_vell","target_character_id":"chr_seren_dask","relationship_type":"opponent","description":"Bram needs toll revenue for bridge safety, but opposes Seren's rising charges because they give the Cartel leverage over Warden work and crossing crews."},{"id":"rel_ila_tamsin","source_character_id":"chr_ila_marr","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reeve","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ila shares harvest and shipment records with Tamsin, while insisting that the cartographer represent the Hollow Circle's needs rather than treating grain as just another route entry."},{"id":"rel_tamsin_bram","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reeve","target_character_id":"chr_bram_vell","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Bram teaches Tamsin to check a chart against the physical condition of the cloudstone; she presses him to account for how toll decisions affect the workers who maintain it."}]}
</Output>
