s the windmills of The Hollow working through uneven currents and remembers how the Great Calm taught the isle to rely on its own stores. She is wiry, sun-browned, and usually carries a tally slate dusted with grain. Her careful records make her a trusted voice among farmers, though her suspicion of outside arrangements can isolate the people she means to protect.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"Protect the food stores and bargaining power that let The Hollow survive disruptions.","goal":"Resist the Cartel grain levy without cutting off the archipelago's legitimate access to food.","flaw":"She equates compromise with surrender and keeps crucial information within the Circle for too long.","internal_conflict":"Ila wants her community to remain self-reliant, but understands that isolation can make other isles vulnerable and leave The Hollow alone against the Cartel.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's levy on grain shipments threatens the Hollow Circle's control of its harvest, while the Toll War makes every crossing more costly.","arc":"Ila begins determined to answer the levy with a blanket refusal to ship grain. When the Cartel's toll dispute threatens to obstruct necessary deliveries, she chooses to share the Circle's harvest tallies with Tamsin and negotiate a limited shipment on transparent terms. She ends better able to distinguish cooperation from capitulation, addressing the secrecy and inflexibility that weakened her position.","personality_traits":["resourceful","steadfast","suspicious","communal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Harvest accounting","description":"Can track stores, mill output, and shipment shares closely enough to expose unfair levies without risking the community's reserves.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_tamsin_seren","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reeve","target_character_id":"chr_seren_dask","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tamsin's route evidence challenges Seren's Cartel-approved records; each sees the other's version of the crossings as a threat to the people who rely on it."},{"id":"rel_bram_seren","source_character_id":"chr_bram_vell","target_character_id":"chr_seren_dask","relationship_type":"opponent","description":"Bram needs toll revenue for bridge safety, but opposes Seren's rising charges because they give the Cartel leverage over Warden work and crossing crews."},{"id":"rel_ila_tamsin","source_character_id":"chr_ila_marr","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reeve","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ila shares harvest and shipment records with Tamsin, while insisting that the cartographer represent the Hollow Circle's needs rather than treating grain as just another route entry."},{"id":"rel_tamsin_bram","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reeve","target_character_id":"chr_bram_vell","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Bram teaches Tamsin to check a chart against the physical condition of the cloudstone; she presses him to account for how toll decisions affect the workers who maintain it."}]}
