ection, he must choose between protecting the order of the records and signing a public safety report with Tamsin. He signs and supplies the repair history, ending as a mentor who still values careful procedure but no longer lets procedure become an excuse for silence.","personality_traits":["patient","cautious","wry","steadfast"],"abilities":[{"name":"Repair memory","description":"Recalls past cable repairs and can connect present strain patterns to earlier maintenance records.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Warden mediation","description":"Helps engineers resolve disagreements by grounding discussion in safety duties and recorded obligations.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_tamsin_vesper","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reed","target_character_id":"chr_vesper_quill","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tamsin Reed distrusts Vesper Quill's Cartel toll plan, while Vesper sees Tamsin's inspections as a threat to a schedule meant to keep trade moving; each needs the other's evidence to prevent a dangerous decision."},{"id":"rel_orin_tamsin","source_character_id":"chr_orin_pell","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reed","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Orin Pell mentored Tamsin Reed in cable inspection and Warden duty, but his cautious loyalty to the institution clashes with her willingness to challenge its neutrality."},{"id":"rel_vesper_orin","source_character_id":"chr_vesper_quill","target_character_id":"chr_orin_pell","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Vesper Quill needs Orin Pell's Warden certification for the Cartel schedule, while Orin distrusts Vesper's tidy accounts until they include the full cost of bridge safety."}]}
