peting obligations, though she must resist concealing her own intentions.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_dain_orrick","name":"Dain Orrick","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","description":"A claimant from a second royal house, Dain grew up among the shipping ledgers and hard bargains of Mistral Docks. His family’s ties to the Drift Cartel taught him that whoever controls passage between islands can make kings of merchants and beggars of their rivals. He dresses in immaculate layered coats suited to the docks' crosswinds and wears a brass tally ring used to mark his family's contracts.","motivation":"Make the archipelago secure by placing its trade and political authority under one decisive ruler.","goal":"Take the throne and preserve the Cartel's control over the shipping lanes and skybridge tolls.","flaw":"He mistakes dependence for loyalty and believes every alliance can be secured by making the other party need him.","internal_conflict":"Dain wants a united realm but cannot accept unity unless he is the one holding its reins.","external_conflict":"Maera challenges his claim, the Bridge Wardens resist rising tolls, and the threat beneath the ice could destroy the trade network his power depends on.","arc":"Dain begins certain that consolidating tolls and authority is the only way to unite the isles. When the enemy beneath the ice threatens the lanes and Maera refuses to bargain away Warden safety, he must choose between extracting a short-term advantage and helping keep the bridges intact. He commits Cartel ships and stores without demanding sole command, ending the story still ambitious but no longer treating every ally as a debtor.","personality_traits":["calculating","charming","ambitious","possessive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Trade leverage","description":"Uses knowledge of cargoes, debts, and shipping schedules to shape negotiations.","category":"social"},{"name":"Ledger memory","description":"Recalls 