eight or wind a bridge can safely withstand.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_the_white_regent","name":"The White Regent","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","description":"An ancient enemy sealed beneath the ice below The Hollow, the White Regent has endured through ages of drifting islands and changing rulers. Its shape is only partly human: a tall silhouette beneath a crust of frost, with pale light where a face should be and ice branching from its shoulders like a crown. It remembers the old realm as something it once ruled and regards the present archipelago as a scattered inheritance to be reclaimed.","motivation":"Restore its dominion over the realm and punish those who built a life above its prison.","goal":"Break free from the ice and turn the rival houses' struggle into an opening for its return.","flaw":"It believes fear and obedience are the only bonds that can hold a realm together.","internal_conflict":"The White Regent claims to seek order, but its need to dominate makes it incapable of recognizing the living archipelago as anything but property.","external_conflict":"Its awakening threatens the isles and skybridges, while the claimants' conflict keeps them from organizing a united defense.","arc":"The White Regent begins its awakening convinced that the rival houses will fracture Aetheria enough for it to reclaim command. When Maera, Sella, and Orrin coordinate the defense across their competing obligations, it chooses to intensify its threat rather than bargain or retreat. That choice exposes its dependence on division; by the end it is forced back beneath the ice, still powerful but no longer able to mistake fear for lasting unity.","personality_traits":["ancient","commanding","vengeful","unyielding"],"abilities":[{"name":"Icebound influence","description":"Extends its awakening through the ice that holds it beneath The Hollow.","category":"supernatural"},{"name":"Whisper of dominion","description":"Magnifies suspicion between rivals by invoking old grievances and the promise of absolute order.","category":"supernatural"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_maera_dain","source_character_id":"chr_maera_veyr","target_character_id":"chr_dain_orrick","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Maera Veyr and Dain Orrick are rival claimants; Maera fears his Cartel-backed tolls will fracture the realm, while Dain sees her as a threat to his plan for centralized rule."},{"id":"rel_sella_dain","source_character_id":"chr_sella_harrow","target_character_id":"chr_dain_orrick","relationship_type":"opponent","description":"Sella Harrow opposes Dain Orrick's grain levy, which she believes makes the Hollow Circle's food supply a tool of Cartel power."},{"id":"rel_orrin_maera","source_character_id":"chr_orrin_tal","target_character_id":"chr_maera_veyr","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Orrin Tal trusts Maera Veyr to take the threat to the skybridges seriously, but he insists that she respect the Wardens' safety requirements."},{"id":"rel_white_regent_maera","source_character_id":"chr_the_white_regent","target_character_id":"chr_maera_veyr","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"The White Regent sees Maera Veyr's effort to unite the claimants as the chief obstacle to exploiting their succession struggle."},{"id":"rel_sella_maera","source_character_id":"chr_sella_harrow","target_character_id":"chr_maera_veyr","relationship_type":"cautious_ally","description":"Sella Harrow supports Maera Veyr's defense effort but holds her to the promise that the Hollow Circle's grain will not be taken without consent."}]}
