 to anticipate likely movement between the isles.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Institutional leverage","description":"Can use corporate access and carefully framed arguments to pressure officials and merchants.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsinro","name":"Tamsin Ro","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","description":"Tamsin Ro is a Bridge Warden engineer from Emberroost, raised around cloudstone cables and the rule that a careless spark can endanger an entire crossing. They have spent years patching damage left by hurried traffic and disputed tolls. Tamsin is broad-shouldered, with soot-darkened sleeves, a close-cropped head, and a brass measuring clasp used to check the tension of bridge braids.","motivation":"To keep the skybridges safe for the people who depend on them, rather than merely profitable for those who control passage.","goal":"Verify the seed's evidence and prevent the corporation or the Drift Cartel from using it to dictate bridge traffic.","flaw":"Tamsin follows procedure so rigidly that they can mistake delay for responsibility.","internal_conflict":"They believe the Wardens must remain impartial, yet neutrality can protect powerful interests when ordinary travelers bear the cost.","external_conflict":"The Toll War strains the Wardens' authority, and helping Nix could expose Tamsin and their colleagues to retaliation from the corporation and the Cartel.","arc":"Tamsin begins determined to keep the Wardens outside Nix's dispute until every claim is verified. When corporate pursuit threatens a skybridge crossing and Nix offers evidence that could help identify the danger, Tamsin must choose between waiting for formal approval and protecting travelers immediately. They act to secure the crossing and carry the evidence forward, ending more willing to challenge procedure when it shields those who endanger the bridges.","personality_traits":["patient","principled","practical","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone repair","description":"Can assess and repair braided skybridge cables while accounting for load and wind strain.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Structural judgment","description":"Recognizes signs of unsafe tension and damage before they become visible failures.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_ilofern","name":"Ilo Fern","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","description":"Ilo Fern is a miller and organizer of the Hollow Circle, raised on the agricultural isle whose windmills feed much of the archipelago. They know that a delayed grain shipment can be as dangerous as a broken bridge, and have kept careful records of levies and deliveries. Ilo has a weather-lined face, flour-white cuffs, and a patched green scarf they use to cover their mouth when the millstones run.","motivation":"To protect the Hollow's food supply from becoming leverage for merchants or corporations.","goal":"Get an honest account of the corporation's shipping records into the hands of people who can challenge the Cartel's grain levy.","flaw":"Ilo avoids direct confrontation, hoping that careful records will persuade even those who profit from ignoring them.","internal_conflict":"They want to keep the Hollow self-reliant but know that refusing all outside help can leave the isle isolated.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's levy threatens grain shipments, while the corporation's pursuit makes anyone who carries Nix's evidence a target.","arc":"Ilo begins relying on records and quiet refusals to resist the grain levy. When the Cartel's demands put a shipment at risk and Nix arrives with evidence linking corporate forecasts to shipping pressure, Ilo chooses to release the records publicly through the available trade network rather than keep them safe and private. They end prepared to defend the Hollow openly while still valuing the careful accounting that makes its case credible.","personality_traits":["measured","generous","cautious","persistent"],"abilities":[{"name":"Supply accounting","description":"Tracks grain stores, shipments, and levies closely enough to spot inconsistencies.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Community organizing","description":"Builds cooperation among farmers and millers without relying on formal authority.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_nix_seren","source_character_id":"chr_nixvale","target_character_id":"chr_serenvaul","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Nix Vale stole the AI seed Seren Vaul is ordered to recover; each sees the other's choices as proof that the other is endangering the archipelago."},{"id":"rel_seren_tamsin","source_character_id":"chr_serenvaul","target_character_id":"chr_tamsinro","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Seren Vaul wants centralized corporate control of route data, while Tamsin Ro defends the Bridge Wardens' responsibility to keep crossings safe without serving private interests."},{"id":"rel_nix_tamsin","source_character_id":"chr_nixvale","target_character_id":"chr_tamsinro","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Nix Vale needs Tamsin Ro's bridge expertise and standing, while Tamsin distrusts Nix's secrecy and must decide whether their evidence is worth the risk."},{"id":"rel_nix_ilo","source_character_id":"chr_nixvale","target_character_id":"chr_ilofern","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ilo Fern helps Nix Vale connect the stolen records to the Cartel's grain levy, but insists that Nix's evidence serve the people whose shipments it exposes."}]}
