ment and its maintenance records.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Careful interviewing","description":"Asks precise questions and remembers small discrepancies in people's accounts.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_mira_quill","name":"Mira Quill","role":"antagonist","description":"Mira is a Drift Cartel ledger-keeper who came to the manor as Oren Pell's discreet assistant. Raised around the busy Mistral Docks, she learned to make figures look tidy even when the trade behind them was not. She is tall and still, with close-cropped dark hair, a slate-grey travel coat, and a brass tally pencil tucked into her sleeve. Mira killed Oren after he discovered that she had altered grain-levy and wind-debt accounts for her own benefit; she now tries to steer suspicion toward the Hollow Circle.","motivation":"Keep her fraud and the murder hidden from the Cartel and the other guests.","goal":"Make the murder appear to be an act of retaliation by someone resisting the grain levy.","flaw":"She believes every person can be controlled if their debts and incentives are understood.","internal_conflict":"Mira resents being treated as a disposable clerk, yet fears that admitting her choices will prove she is no more than the role the Cartel gave her.","external_conflict":"Elowen's questions and the guests' conflicting memories threaten to expose the altered accounts and Mira's opportunity to reach Oren alone.","arc":"Mira begins the weekend convinced she can manage the truth as neatly as a ledger; when Elowen finds the false wind-debt entry and Ivo refuses to let her redirect blame onto the Hollow Circle, Mira must choose between confessing and escalating her lies. She tries to preserve her control, is exposed, and ends the story facing the consequences of the murder rather than hiding behind her clerical position.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","personality_traits":["composed","calculating","meticulous","defensive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger analysis","description":"Tracks discrepancies across shipping, grain, and wind-debt accounts.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Social masking","description":"Maintains a calm, helpful manner while concealing what she knows.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_oren_pell","name":"Oren Pell","role":"supporting","description":"Oren was a senior Drift Cartel collector whose polished manners concealed an appetite for leverage. He had come from Mistral Docks to press the Hollow Circle over grain shipments and wind-debt payments, and brought a private ledger that recorded more than the official accounts. He was broad-shouldered, carefully groomed, and always wore a blue enamel pin marking his Cartel office. His murder turns the manor gathering into an uneasy investigation and gives the other characters a reason to confront what they owe one another.","motivation":"Preserve his standing in the Cartel by keeping control of the records and people he has pressured.","goal":"Secure agreement to the Cartel's grain levy before leaving the Hollow.","flaw":"He treats personal trust as another resource to extract and mistakes fear for loyalty.","internal_conflict":"Oren wants recognition as more than a collector, but cannot imagine earning it without wielding the authority of the Cartel.","external_conflict":"The Hollow Circle resists his levy, the Wardens question the fairness of the tolls, and Mira knows that his private ledger could expose her falsifications.","arc":"Oren begins the weekend certain that his Cartel authority will force agreement; when Elowen challenges the ledger's treatment of wind-debt and the Hollow Circle refuses his terms, he briefly considers revealing how the accounts were manipulated to protect his own position. Before he can make that choice, Mira murders him, leaving his private records to undermine the leverage he spent the weekend asserting.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","personality_traits":["charming","domineering","status-conscious","shrewd"],"abilities":[{"name":"Trade negotiation","description":"Uses debts, schedules, and shipping terms to pressure merchants into agreements.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ivo_tarn","name":"Ivo Tarn","role":"supporting","description":"Ivo is a Bridge Warden engineer invited to the manor to advise on a disputed crossing and its accumulated wind-debt. He has spent most of his life between Emberroost's forge-island and Silverspine's charts, and is more comfortable with a cable under strain than with a room full of guests. His rangy build, copper spectacles, and weather-scuffed coat make him look perpetually fresh from an inspection. He and Mira once cooperated on toll records, a connection neither is eager to discuss after Oren's death.","motivation":"Keep the skybridge network safe and its maintenance obligations honest.","goal":"Show that the Cartel's account of the Hollow's wind-debt does not match the bridge records.","flaw":"He hides behind technical language when a moral judgment or personal risk is required.","internal_conflict":"Ivo believes impartial rules protect everyone, but has seen the Wardens' records used to excuse unfair tolls.","external_conflict":"His prior work with Mira makes him a convenient suspect, and the Cartel may use any bridge-record dispute to weaken the Wardens.","arc":"Ivo begins the weekend insisting that only verified engineering records matter; when Elowen finds the altered entry and Mira tries to frame the Hollow Circle, he chooses to explain his past cooperation openly and identify the record he approved without proper scrutiny. He ends willing to own his part in the dispute and to testify plainly rather than shelter behind technicalities.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","personality_traits":["methodical","reserved","conscientious","literal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable assessment","description":"Evaluates bridge strain and recognizes signs of repair or tampering.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Record verification","description":"Compares maintenance notes and crossing records against Warden procedures.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_sella_bram","name":"Sella Bram","role":"supporting","description":"Sella is a Hollow Circle miller whose family has supplied grain through both calm seasons and shifting winds. She attends the manor party to negotiate a fairer shipment arrangement, not to make friends with the Cartel. She is sturdy and broad-faced, with flour caught in the seams of her green sleeves and an easy laugh that disappears when someone speaks for the Circle without asking. She knows the guests' habits from preparing the gathering and is one of the first people Mira tries to cast suspicion upon.","motivation":"Keep the Circle's grain in local hands and prevent the levy from making the mills dependent on Cartel favor.","goal":"Leave the gathering with a fair shipment agreement and the Circle's reputation intact.","flaw":"Her fierce independence makes her refuse help even when shared effort would protect her neighbors.","internal_conflict":"Sella wants the Hollow Circle to stand together, but worries that compromise will let outsiders decide the terms of their survival.","external_conflict":"Oren's levy threatens the Circle's livelihood, and Mira's attempt to blame a local miller puts Sella and her community under suspicion.","arc":"Sella begins the weekend ready to reject every offer from the Cartel; after Oren's murder, Mira's accusation threatens to isolate her, so Sella chooses to share the Circle's shipment notes with Elowen and explain which records the millers keep collectively. She ends prepared to negotiate as a group, preserving independence without mistaking cooperation for surrender.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","personality_traits":["forthright","generous","stubborn","community-minded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Mill operations","description":"Understands grain storage, milling schedules, and the practical details of local shipments.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Community organizing","description":"Brings neighbors together around shared work and collective decisions.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_elowen_mira","source_character_id":"chr_elowen_vale","target_character_id":"chr_mira_quill","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Elowen investigates Oren's murder while Mira tries to redirect her questions toward the Hollow Circle."},{"id":"rel_mira_ivo","source_character_id":"chr_mira_quill","target_character_id":"chr_ivo_tarn","relationship_type":"former allies","description":"Mira and Ivo once worked together on toll records; their shared history gives Mira leverage and makes Ivo reluctant to reveal what he approved."},{"id":"rel_sella_oren","source_character_id":"chr_sella_bram","target_character_id":"chr_oren_pell","relationship_type":"opponents","description":"Sella resists Oren's grain levy, while Oren uses Cartel authority to pressure her community."},{"id":"rel_elowen_sella","source_character_id":"chr_elowen_vale","target_character_id":"chr_sella_bram","relationship_type":"friends","description":"Elowen and Sella trust one another as Hollow neighbors, though Sella challenges Elowen when she tries to protect the Circle without consulting it."},{"id":"rel_oren_mira","source_character_id":"chr_oren_pell","target_character_id":"chr_mira_quill","relationship_type":"uneasy colleagues","description":"Oren relies on Mira to keep the Cartel accounts, while Mira fears he will expose her falsifications."}]}
