ment and its maintenance records.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Careful interviewing","description":"Asks precise questions and remembers small discrepancies in people's accounts.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_mira_quill","name":"Mira Quill","role":"antagonist","description":"Mira is a Drift Cartel ledger-keeper who came to the manor as Oren Pell's discreet assistant. Raised around the busy Mistral Docks, she learned to make figures look tidy even when the trade behind them was not. She is tall and still, with close-cropped dark hair, a slate-grey travel coat, and a brass tally pencil tucked into her sleeve. Mira killed Oren after he discovered that she had altered grain-levy and wind-debt accounts for her own benefit; she now tries to steer suspicion toward the Hollow Circle.","motivation":"Keep her fraud and the murder hidden from the Cartel and the other guests.","goal":"Make the murder appear to be an act of retaliation by someone resisting the grain levy.","flaw":"She believes every person can be controlled if their debts and incentives are understood.","internal_conflict":"Mira resents being treated as a disposable clerk, yet fears that admitting her choices will prove she is no more than the role the Cartel gave her.","external_conflict":"Elowen's questions and the guests' conflicting memories threaten to expose the altered accounts and Mira's opportunity to reach Oren alone.","arc":"Mira begins the weekend convinced she can manage the truth as neatly as a ledger; when Elowen finds the false wind-debt entry and Ivo refuses to let her redirect blame onto the Hollow Circle, Mira must choose between confessing and escalating her lies. She tries to preserve her control, is exposed, and ends the story facing the consequences of the murder rather than hiding behind her clerical position.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","personality_traits":["composed","calculating","meticulous","defensive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger 