 voices, interference, and repeated patterns by ear after years of live broadcasting.","category":"technological"},{"name":"On-air composure","description":"Can keep her voice measured during a broadcast even when frightened, helping listeners stay focused.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle"},{"id":"chr_nera_voss_future","name":"Nera Voss, the Returning Voice","role":"antagonist","description":"The Returning Voice is Nera as she sounds through the radio: older, hoarse, and worn down by nights spent repeating the same warnings. Her words arrive from a future Nera cannot verify, threaded with the faint crackle of a signal struggling across distance or time. She claims that every catastrophe began with one small choice in the cabin and insists that the present Nera must follow her instructions exactly. Though she shares Nera's measured cadence, her pauses are too deliberate, as if she is listening for an answer from a room that has been empty for years.","motivation":"She wants to prevent the disaster she remembers, even if preserving the future requires stripping her earlier self of choice.","goal":"Make the present Nera follow her sequence of warnings and keep the broadcast from revealing information she believes will trigger the catastrophe.","flaw":"She mistakes having survived an outcome for proof that her choices were the only possible ones.","internal_conflict":"She cannot tell whether she is protecting her former self or trying to justify the secrecy and sacrifices that shaped her own past.","external_conflict":"Her warnings reach the cabin before the events they describe, but each attempt to direct Nera deepens suspicion and risks turning a useful broadcast into a source of panic.","arc":"The Returning Voice begins convinced that repetition and control are the only ways to prevent disaster. When the present Nera publicly shares a warning instead of obeying the instruction to hide it, the Returning Voice 