[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_vane","name":"Mara Vane","role":"protagonist","description":"Mara Vane is a former pirate captain who once ran contraband through the skybridges and knows how quickly a friendly port can become a trap. After leaving piracy, she has tried to repay the wind-debts her crew left behind by working honest passages from Mistral Docks. She is lean and weather-browned, with a cloudstone clasp replacing a missing tooth and a faded sailmaker's compass tattooed on her wrist. The stolen map is a cartographer's chart of shifting bridge routes; Mara recognizes the marks as a key to passages the Drift Cartel wants kept under its control.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"Prove that changing her life means more than merely escaping the consequences of her old one.","goal":"Recover the stolen route map before the Cartel uses it to tighten its grip on trade between the isles.","flaw":"She treats every alliance as a temporary bargain and withholds information until she can control the outcome.","internal_conflict":"Mara fears that the ruthless instincts that made her a successful pirate are the only ones capable of keeping her alive.","external_conflict":"The Cartel has branded her a thief again, while its agents and the Wardens both want the map for competing reasons; every skybridge crossing also adds wind-debt she cannot afford to ignore.","arc":"Mara begins by pursuing the map alone and planning to sell its contents for enough money to erase her debts. When the Cartel threatens to seize the Hollow Circle's grain shipments using a route exposed by the map, she chooses to entrust the chart to the Wardens and help them recover it instead of bargaining for herself. She ends as a reformed captain willing to share control and accept responsibility for the people her choices put at risk.","personality_traits":["resourceful","wary","quick-witted","restless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Sky-lane instinct","description":"Reads wind shifts, sail signals, and the telltale wear on bridge cables to choose safer passages through the drifting isles.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Boarding reflexes","description":"Uses practiced balance and close-quarters footwork learned in her pirate years, though she avoids fighting when escape is possible.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_orrin_vale","name":"Orrin Vale","role":"antagonist","description":"Orrin Vale is a polished factor of the Drift Cartel who rose from a dockside tally clerk to the prince's trusted keeper of shipping accounts. He believes the archipelago's fragile trade can survive only when one authority controls its routes and tolls. His immaculate dark coat bears a silver route-pin, and his hands are ink-stained despite his careful manners. Orrin arranged the theft of the map from Silverspine Academy, intending to identify alternate crossings and make the Cartel's tolls unavoidable.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"Keep the archipelago from returning to the disorder he associates with the Great Calm.","goal":"Use the stolen map to secure Cartel control over the most reliable skybridge routes.","flaw":"He mistakes obedience for stability and assumes people will accept any hardship if it is presented as necessary.","internal_conflict":"Orrin privately knows that the Cartel's rising tolls are deepening the very scarcity and resentment he claims to prevent.","external_conflict":"Mara is pursuing the map, the Bridge Wardens oppose Cartel interference with their network, and the Hollow Circle resists a grain levy that Orrin needs to fund his shipping plan.","arc":"Orrin begins convinced that secrecy and rising tolls are the price of keeping trade orderly. When Mara exposes that his planned routes would force grain shipments through Cartel-controlled crossings, he must choose between silencing her and publicly accounting for the levy. He releases the map's toll calculations to the Wardens and accepts a loss of authority, ending as a constrained negotiator rather than an unquestioned controller.","personality_traits":["methodical","persuasive","proud","anxious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Trade arithmetic","description":"Can quickly calculate the costs, dependencies, and leverage hidden in shipping ledgers and toll agreements.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Courtly negotiation","description":"Uses precise language and careful concessions to make coercive proposals sound like mutual agreements.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tavi_quill","name":"Tavi Quill","role":"supporting","description":"Tavi Quill is a junior cartographer at Silverspine Academy, raised among maps that must be corrected whenever the islands drift or a bridge is repaired. They helped copy the stolen chart and recognized a small sequence of marks that reveals its route annotations were altered. Tavi is compact and sharp-eyed, with wind-tangled hair, blue ink on their cuffs, and a case of mapmaking tools worn smooth from use. They are loyal to the Bridge Wardens but uneasy about how readily their work can be used to justify tolls or block access.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"Protect the trustworthiness of maps and the people who rely on them to cross safely.","goal":"Help Mara locate the stolen chart's true route marks and return an accurate copy to the Wardens.","flaw":"They hide behind technical precision when a situation calls for taking a moral risk.","internal_conflict":"Tavi fears that choosing a side will make their careful work serve power rather than truth.","external_conflict":"The Cartel wants their knowledge of the chart's revisions, while the Wardens need them to verify routes before the map can be safely recovered or shared.","arc":"Tavi begins by refusing to disclose anything beyond verified measurements, hoping neutrality will keep the map out of factional hands. When a Cartel agent corners them at Silverspine and demands the unrevised route key, Tavi sends Mara a corrected copy despite knowing it will reveal their involvement. They end willing to put accurate knowledge into responsible hands and answer publicly for the choice.","personality_traits":["observant","patient","exacting","conflict-averse"],"abilities":[{"name":"Route reconstruction","description":"Compares bridge records, drift observations, and map annotations to identify altered or outdated passages.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_sella_morn","name":"Sella Morn","role":"supporting","description":"Sella Morn is a miller and elected voice of the Hollow Circle, responsible for coordinating grain shipments when the islands' drift makes delivery schedules uncertain. She remembers how the Great Calm taught the Hollow to feed itself, and she distrusts anyone who treats food as leverage. Broad-shouldered and silver-haired, she wears a flour-dusted apron over patched traveling clothes and carries a small ledger of promised grain shares. Sella is not a fighter, but she knows which shipment can be delayed without starving a settlement and which cannot.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"Keep food accessible to every settlement, even when powerful factions use shortages to demand concessions.","goal":"Stop the Cartel's grain levy from turning essential shipments into another toll-controlled route.","flaw":"She carries every burden herself and can mistake refusing help for protecting her people.","internal_conflict":"Sella fears that depending on outsiders will leave the Hollow Circle vulnerable to the same control it resists.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's levy threatens the Circle's grain deliveries, and Mara's search for the map could bring Cartel reprisals to the Hollow.","arc":"Sella begins by hiding the Circle's reserve stores and refusing to involve Mara, believing secrecy is the only safe defense against the Cartel. When the levy threatens a shipment needed by several isles, she chooses to disclose the Circle's route and stores to the Wardens so they can help protect the crossing. She ends still fiercely independent, but willing to share responsibility rather than make the Hollow bear the risk alone.","personality_traits":["steadfast","practical","protective","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Supply planning","description":"Tracks stores, milling capacity, and delivery needs well enough to spot when a levy or delay will cause real scarcity.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Community mediation","description":"Settles disputes among farmers and millers by finding workable shares before disagreements become factional fractures.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_orrin","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vane","target_character_id":"chr_orrin_vale","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Mara Vane and Orrin Vale are adversaries: she seeks the map to prevent the Cartel from monopolizing routes, while he wants it to make that control enforceable."},{"id":"rel_mara_tavi","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vane","target_character_id":"chr_tavi_quill","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mara Vane relies on Tavi Quill to distinguish the chart's true route marks from Cartel alterations, while Tavi tests whether Mara can be trusted with dangerous information."},{"id":"rel_tavi_sella","source_character_id":"chr_tavi_quill","target_character_id":"chr_sella_morn","relationship_type":"friend","description":"Tavi Quill and Sella Morn have worked together to keep route records useful for the Hollow's grain deliveries; Sella urges Tavi to consider who bears the cost when maps stay secret."},{"id":"rel_sella_orrin","source_character_id":"chr_sella_morn","target_character_id":"chr_orrin_vale","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Sella Morn opposes Orrin Vale's grain levy, which she sees as using food shipments to force the Hollow Circle under Cartel control."}]}
</Output>
